   "source": [
    "#### Problem 2.1 - Low level gradient calculation: The most simple way is to approximate the gradient\n",
    "as the difference between neighboring pixels/voxels.\n",
    "In a 1D signal, x, this would be:\n",
    "MATLAB: dx = x(2:end) - x(1:end-1)\n",
    "PYTHON: dx = x[1:] - x[0:-1]\n",
    "Obtain Vx,Vy,Vt for the entire volume and display for some selected frames.\n",
    "Consider what happens with the image/volume size, when performing gradient calculations like this?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "d3083a4a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "frames.shape"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "484995d4",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "V = frames[1:, 1:, 1:] - frames[:-1, :-1, :-1]\n",
    "\n",
    "# frame = V[50, :, :]\n",
    "Vx_raw = frames[:, :, 1:] - frames[:, :, :-1]\n",
    "Vy_raw = frames[:, 1:, :] - frames[:, :-1, :]\n",
    "Vt_raw = frames[1:, :, :] - frames[:-1, :, :]\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure()\n",
    "plt.imshow(Vx_raw[50], cmap=\"gray\")\n",
    "plt.title(\"Optical Flow (Frame 1)\")\n",
    "plt.axis(\"off\")\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
