   "source": [
    "Conclusions:\n",
    "* axis=0, means horizontal kernel (alongside rows)\n",
    "* axis=1 means vertical kernel (alongside columns)\n",
    "* batching does not work (cannot do this with 3 at the same time haha, at least when the time is first)\n",
    "* Flipping - for kernels like sobel and prewit, it's simply about taking a negative.\n",
    "* To actually understand the underlying implementation - I would need to spend some time on the underlying logic."
   ]
